# RHCSA Exam Question No 14

==========================================

Configure the system so that all new users passwords must be at least 9 characters long and also expire after 30 days.
`chage -l username` to check some password details.

Steps:

vim /etc/login.defs, change PASS_MAX_DAYS to 30
We need to change the value of "Maximum number of days between password changes"
find /etc -type f -name "*pwquality*" (if you cant remember where this file is)
vim /etc/security/pwquality.conf
In the 9th or 10th line, change minlen = 8 to minlen = 10
Test by adding a user, and chage -l new_user, (Maximum no of days should be 30) and then `passwd new_user`